      ],
      "source": "https://southeastmontana.com/community/huntley",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1905 the U.S. Bureau of Reclamation began the Huntley Project, an irrigation scheme on former Crow Reservation land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntley%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1937 Yellowstone Flood forced Huntley to relocate from the north bank to higher ground on the south bank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
